#edb/ref 17592186390639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49b051d2-a870-54d8-b0d0-bc062f6639ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390643} {:answer/id #uuid "37807bee-a3e2-5e2b-8818-a45a3dd0dd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37807bee-a3e2-5e2b-8818-a45a3dd0dd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390644} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e7f583d-2860-5e37-8901-180f3f0e774b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5518c6eb-7003-5091-9fd8-e6bce291454f" :question/math-academy-id "q-317169" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{5}.$ Fill the table with appropriate sign of $f(x,y)$ as shown below.\n\n| $y>0$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd85410238231152b6f905921f594af15293d6efc54b0b1ce558131a05bf6ee.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/e9/e95107f16eb80a06cd172c30ec78992838f974a91f9f2fa17b7c8ac77125c438.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | ${x}^{3}$ | ${y}^{5}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/36/36e292eea1cf0be1527b2a357f1939e4c95f0202aa0ce5b91e9079da493f2155.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f61a7c3-82e6-5f90-8a95-4a79078fd542" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Growth Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a771d975-2aaa-513d-bcb8-8905d9edc2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/5559cd21367ed24058d7f0a3f1f646feb6cbdc269cbd4128788b17cbd331a01e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390647} {:answer/id #uuid "41d7c55e-75b0-54d8-907f-70f90a5594aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b05cb7e1d42380d1a1ac76139b39bbed49f429dbc43fddbae79b47e61d5659fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390648} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd1f9e6-af1e-5909-94b9-5f25d90a06ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30b885e19455654b28e87aba56427a82bfb9abe98d28dc5b542214a7fd55315f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390649} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4ddff0-6b9c-5567-88cf-552367429984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7fbb4a84bc3fa077711d003c7b05fa8bccfb84b31a112736363fa4de00315e54.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390650} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ef6180-669c-546a-a8a2-ed7f728e356b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/7868ed246bfad0cbcb848098c39443616acf8554620537ad5cf53fa46fdaf9e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dd1f9e6-af1e-5909-94b9-5f25d90a06ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30b885e19455654b28e87aba56427a82bfb9abe98d28dc5b542214a7fd55315f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390649} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9df4524-7dfb-5370-9bcc-d5a8bffd76f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6b5ac66-3c43-5e20-bd0d-692b07d708ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-317281" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{3}^{x}+1?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={3}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/17/17a76468bd4f446f420d784ae479724135b2af3369a7d69f87c67507e74a8901.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{3}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/ac/ac5e769c069b753bbf3f6a9a276b69881a3d2699afc4f62498233ecc526f5a2b.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $1$ unit up to give $y=-{3}^{x}+1.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,0)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=1.$\n\n![](images/c6/c69c8be5828709cef483cba56d5842b973cf718e7592a8fba9e825be08204f5b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f61a7c3-82e6-5f90-8a95-4a79078fd542" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Growth Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6201916-ff41-54d1-97cf-62c6516a067d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f95a21987377cae131f3d627ae1dc5156f4871a73cae4fec667521f3e66fcf7c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390654} {:answer/id #uuid "5e48d6e0-ded7-563c-8901-966cfafd124e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/469aaa6b3110693e02dfd987c104169c603a73c69782ec491700ea7d250103a7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390655} {:answer/id #uuid "70cf48de-781d-5c0e-b225-b89c2b1f1b54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1c/1c31f62568e601154d960de5d0a046ad9e1aeb4fa5eafefcd82abb4205797c77.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390656} {:answer/id #uuid "f38fc2a2-80f0-5cf9-a37f-f2e0720c822a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/227aa9ad8e6d95c99e3984ce9959de38d7ca50c98111e5ba94c0a8036a7a5f8e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390657} {:answer/id #uuid "00d16dba-cc93-521a-afbe-d86f7d117e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d4811fb906db8a9326ae35826aa5ab2b3795d890c7a5f21862419206cecbcf83.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e48d6e0-ded7-563c-8901-966cfafd124e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/469aaa6b3110693e02dfd987c104169c603a73c69782ec491700ea7d250103a7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390655} :answer-field/id #uuid "db4f0261-516d-5ca8-9751-c4b35539e35a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72b43272-13a0-5f4c-969a-26359e69928e" :question/math-academy-id "q-317285" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{2}^{x}-4?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={2}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/2f/2fe0fb3f0f5d302d39f6ad578148c4973618595452b59fea8a8bb2399ef92ddc.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{2}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(